{
  "about": "Source ranking and line speed rules, shared by the TypeScript tests (packages/core, src/sources/ranking.ts) and the Kotlin commonTest (apps/mobile). Budget = (lineMbps > 0 ? lineMbps : 40) * 0.7. Fit: overBudget when neededMbps > 0 and > budget; else exceedsScreen when screenHeight > 0, quality is known and its nominal height (2160p 2160, 1440p 1440, 1080p 1080, 720p 720, 480p 480, SD 480) > screenHeight * 1.25; else fits. Order: cached === true first; then fits, exceedsScreen, overBudget; inside fits and exceedsScreen higher quality first (2160p, 1440p, 1080p, 720p, 480p, SD, then null), then larger sizeBytes (null as 0); inside overBudget lower neededMbps first, then higher quality; full ties keep input order. Qualities use the parser's vocabulary, so SD is upper case. Line speed: a peak that is not a positive finite number keeps previous (0 stays 0); previous <= 0 takes the peak; a higher peak replaces previous; a stall takes the peak; otherwise previous; results other than 0 are clamped to [0.5, 100000].",
